Explain framing and partial reads in a TCP application protocol.|A receiver assumes one read contains one complete application message. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain when UDP is appropriate and what the application must provide.|A telemetry collector sees gaps in UDP sequence numbers. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the difference between A AAAA and service discovery records.|A client resolves only IPv4 while the intended endpoint is IPv6-only. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain a low-risk DNS migration and rollback plan.|Some clients still reach the old address just after a DNS change. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how subnet masks affect direct versus routed delivery.|Two hosts believed to share a subnet cannot communicate directly. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain route selection and how you would troubleshoot a missing default route.|A host reaches its local subnet but cannot reach external networks. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you distinguish a local neighbor problem from a routing problem.|A host cannot reach a same-subnet peer and its neighbor entry stays incomplete. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the difference between port reachability and service readiness.|A port accepts connections but requests fail immediately. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how to separate TCP TLS and HTTP failures.|TCP connects quickly but HTTPS fails afterward. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain TLS identity validation and safe certificate troubleshooting.|A client reports a certificate hostname mismatch. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how status codes narrow a troubleshooting investigation.|A load balancer returns 503 while targets are marked unhealthy. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain NAT exhaustion and how connection pooling changes the demand.|New outbound connections fail during a connection-rate spike. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain request and response rules for a stateless packet filter.|Requests leave a subnet but stateless rules reject the replies. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain a path MTU black hole and the evidence you would collect.|Small requests work but larger responses stall on a tunneled path. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would determine whether packet loss is causing user-visible latency.|Latency worsens during bursts and retransmissions rise. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain negative DNS caching during a service launch.|A hostname was queried before it existed and still fails at one resolver. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain transport liveness versus application health.|A connection stays established while the application worker is deadlocked. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain connection pooling trade-offs under bursty load.|A service creates a new TLS connection for every short request. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the difference between L4 and L7 load balancing.|Two applications share an address but require routing by URL path. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain secure handling of client identity behind reverse proxies.|An access rule accepts a forged forwarding header from a direct client. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how retry behavior can turn a partial failure into a larger outage.|A dependency slows and callers launch synchronized repeated requests. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain deadlines cancellation and ambiguous outcomes in network calls.|A payment request times out and the client is about to repeat it. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would diagnose asymmetric-path connectivity failures.|Packets reach the server but replies take a different firewall path and disappear. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain anycast benefits and session-continuity risks.|A route change moves traffic to another anycast location. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain why Internet routing may not follow the shortest geographic path.|Traffic follows an unexpected provider path despite a nearby alternative. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain why blanket ICMPv6 blocking is unsafe for IPv6 connectivity.|IPv6 communication breaks after a blanket ICMPv6 deny rule. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain TIME_WAIT and when connection churn becomes a capacity problem.|A busy client creates many short connections and accumulates TIME_WAIT sockets. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain throughput latency and bufferbloat trade-offs.|Throughput looks stable but interactive latency climbs during bulk transfers. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain end-to-end transport protection through a reverse proxy.|A compliance requirement covers traffic between the proxy and backend. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would design retries for a write whose response can be lost.|A client may retry an order after losing the response. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
